What is the value of $y$ in the solution to the system of equations above?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, '1', ARRAY['1'], E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(5x - 3y) + (2x + 3y) = 17 + 11$ gives $7x = 28$, so $x = 4$. Substituting $x = 4$ into $2x + 3y = 11$: $2(4) + 3y = 11$ gives $8 + 3y = 11$, so $3y = 3$ and $y = 1$. Verification: $5(4) - 3(1) = 20 - 3 = 17$ ✓ and $2(4) + 3(1) = 8 + 3 = 11$ ✓.', NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 75, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);



